bodies-in-liquids-answer-ball-text-2 = {" "}In water the ball goes { $s } cm in under a second — hard to time by hand: the finger’s delay (0.1–0.2 s) matters here.
bodies-in-liquids-answer-ball-text-3 = { $steps }. The speed does not follow the density: oil is the lightest, yet the ball is slower in it than in water — because oil is much more viscous.{ $s }
